                <pb facs="0517" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg451"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex 3]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Annex and Supplement on the Part of the Government
                        of the United States</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">IV. Commerce between both
                    nations</hi>.</p>
                <p>It is understood that during the present international emergency Japan and the
                    United States each shall permit export to the other of commodities in amounts up
                    to the figures of usual or pre-war trade, except, in the case of each,
                    commodities which it needs for its own purposes of security and
                    self-defense.</p>
            </div>
